## 4. How to Run the System

### Prerequisites
Ensure Redis is running locally on Windows:
```powershell
# Default Redis port: 127.0.0.1:6379
redis-server
```

### 1. Start Django Backend API
```powershell
cd C:\Users\robel\Desktop\ERP\backend
python manage.py runserver 0.0.0.0:8000
```

### 2. Start Celery Worker (Asynchronous Task Processor)
```powershell
cd C:\Users\robel\Desktop\ERP\backend
.\start-celery-worker.bat
```
*(Executes `celery -A erp worker -l info -P solo`)*

### 3. Start Celery Beat (Periodic Scheduler)
```powershell
cd C:\Users\robel\Desktop\ERP\backend
.\start-celery-beat.bat
```
*(Executes `celery -A erp beat -l info`)*

### 4. Start Slash Admin Frontend
```powershell
cd C:\Users\robel\Desktop\ERP\slash-admin
npm run dev
```
Navigate to `http://localhost:5173` to use the application.
